- Detects the library using `b.findSystemLibrary` if available.
- If not found, fetches a tarball from a URL (specified in `build.zig.zon`) and builds the C library using Zig's built-in C compiler (`b.addCSourceFiles`).
- Links your Zig application against the library (either system or locally built).
- Exposes a idiomatic Zig API that calls the C functions (e.g., `uuid_generate` returning a `std.uuid.Uuid`).

